			"notes": "First public pre-release of MetalCraft: Minecraft 1.21.11 rendered through **native Metal** instead of OpenGL on Apple Silicon.\n\n**Requirements:** Apple Silicon, macOS 14+, Minecraft 1.21.11, Fabric Loader 0.19.5+, Fabric API. Optional: Sodium 0.8.14.\n\n### Highlights\n- Full Blaze3D backend on Metal; no OpenGL context is created.\n- Runtime GLSL → MSL shader translation (vanilla and resource-pack core shaders), cached on disk after the first launch.\n- Sodium 0.8.14 terrain rendering ported to Metal.\n- At a fixed 60 fps (render distance 16): render-thread CPU 12–13% vs 21% on OpenGL; ~4.7 ms GPU per frame (~4.0 ms with Sodium).\n- F3 GPU utilization works.\n\n### Known limitations\n- Pre-release: tested on one machine with a fixed test world. The Nether/End, resource packs and other rendering mods are largely untested.\n- Mods that call OpenGL directly (outside Blaze3D) aren't supported.\n- Color logic ops (not used by vanilla) are ignored.\n\nPlease report issues with your Mac model, macOS version and mod list."
